*Regardless* of the arguments, I'm staunchly against it precisely for the 
fact that people will *use* it. Regardless of whether or not *I* have to 
use it, *other* people will, which means that *I* have to learn to read it. 
Therefore, it *does* affect me, even if I *do* choose to use the original 
sumti connectives. Therefore, I will always veto this idea every time 
forever.

That being said, I will gladly bring it to Robin's attention, who I presume 
will laugh and say, "Fuck no.", but very well may not.
I'll even see about getting video footage of the discussion.

